    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">On a tic-tac-toe board of size <var>n</var>, two players have each placed a piece such that neither piece shares a row or column. The best move in this circumstance is always to place the next piece on one of the two cells that shares its row with one piece and its column with the other.<br><br>Given the current state of the board, where the placed pieces are marked <const>X</const> or <const>O</const> and the remaining cells are represented by their priority values (higher value = higher priority), find the best cell on which to place the next piece, tie breaking based on priority. Return the board after placing <const>X</const> in that cell.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> An integer <var>n</var> for the width and height of the board<br><strong>Next <var>n</var> Lines:</strong> <var>n</var> space-separated values representing a priority value or placed piece for each cell in the row.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong><var>n</var> Lines:</strong> <var>n</var> space-separated values representing a priority value or placed piece for each cell in the row after placing the new piece.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\"><const>3</const>&lt;=<var>n</var>&lt;=<const>9</const><br><const>1</const>&lt;=cell value&lt;=<const><var>n</var>^2</const>   <strong>or</strong>   cell value = <const>X</const> or <const>O</const><br>All cell priority values will be distinct.<br>The board will always contain exactly one <const>X</const> and one <const>O</const>, each placed in differing rows and columns.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">3\n8 4 7\nX 9 2\n6 O 5</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">8 4 7\nX X 2\n6 O 5</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
